From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:52:42 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] WebRender's shader cache on Windows 10 Mobile: notes, a
 refused binary stored again, the startup list kept

The program binary cache already works on the hardware path (HP Elite x3):
a cold compile costs about a second on the second frame, a warm one does
not. Notes now say where the cache is, how many binaries were read and
linked, how long compiles took and what was refused. Fixed upstream bug:
when ANGLE refused a binary the stale entry stayed, so the fresh binary
from the recompile was never stored and the refusal repeated every launch.
The startup list is no longer replaced by an empty one written before any
program is linked. An early warmup in the render thread's idle window is
there behind gfx.webrender.gecko-w10m.shader-warmup-early, off: its gain is
unproven and it competes with the main thread's startup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
